"x64.kfx: kc's native back end, x86-64 (docs/research/kc.md): `asm PATH`,
 assembly for the system's assembler, of `kc_entry`, which gives the
 program's value in `%rax` in Fixpt's format (`fixpt-heap`'s `value.rs`),
 for the runtime (`crates/kayak-kcrt`) to write: a fixnum its value
 shifted past three tag bits, tag 0; an immediate, tag 3, its kind above
 the tag (false 0, true 1, the empty list 2, unit 3, a character 8), its
 payload from bit 8 (a character's code); a pair, the address of its
 cell of two words, car and cdr, tag 1.

 `kc_entry` is given the heap, its first free word and its end, kept in
 `%r12` and `%r13` (callee-saved, so saved and put back): a `cons` takes
 two words from it (C406); past its end, kcrt's collector is called
 (C453, `kc_gc_call`), which moves what kc's stack, the globals' cells
 and the runtime's own pairs reach, every word of the stack read as a
 value, so that each frame is zeroed when made. And a state, kept in `%r15`,
 as Fixpt's native convention keeps one (C451): kc's own convention is
 Fixpt's data and Fixpt's state, its calls its own. Each function's entry
 checks the stack against the state's limit and takes a unit of its fuel,
 calling its `poll` when none is left; a cell is written through the
 state's code distance, so that the same code runs as a built program
 (kayak-kcrt's state, a distance of no pages) and in process, from the
 code area's executable view (`kc run`, kc/native.kfx; its runtime the
 stubs of `x64-run-support`).

 Each term is compiled to code that leaves its value in `%rax` (Ghuloum's
 `emit-expr`, C402); a primitive's first arguments are kept in the frame's
 slots, `8 * i(%rsp)`, while the rest are made (C403), and each variable a
 `let` binds in a slot of its own (C404). `kc_entry`'s frame
 is as many slots as the code uses, and 8 bytes more where that keeps the
 stack aligned for a call (it is entered 8 below a multiple of 16), so
 that a failure may call the runtime's `kc_fail`, which writes Fixpt's
 words and ends the run; each failure's call is out of the line, after the
 `ret`, a check a conditional jump to it.

 A lambda (C412) is a function of its own, out of the line after the
 code that makes it, and a closure of it, Fixpt's bloblet (below); a call
 of a procedure as a value calls its closure's code, the closure in
 `%r10`, whose free values the function first copies to its slots.

 A call in tail position (C413) gives its function's frame back and jumps
 to the callee, which returns to this one's caller: the arguments are all
 in registers, so nothing of the frame is needed after. A function's frame
 is a symbol (`.set` once its code is made), so that each of its returns
 and tail calls may give it back before its size is known.

 Integers are fixnums alone, as yet: an operation whose result would be
 past one fails, `not yet` (until the heap, and big integers on it)."

(define kc-x64
  (module
    (hide
      (import kc-front kc-hex kc-datum kc-items-of kc-keys (type qbody))
      (import kc-l0 not-yet l0-item term-head item-kind item-name item-params item-body call-name call-args var-number let-bindings let-body if-parts seq-terms prim-name prim-args term-number term-text lambda-params lambda-free app-fn app-args gproc-arity tagcase-arms letrec-binders letrec-values)
      (import kc-rust sexp-at))

    (hide
      (define x64-immediate (subr kfx (i64 i64) i64)
        (lambda (kind payload) (i64+ (i64* payload 256) (i64+ (i64* kind 8) 3))))

      (define x64-word-false i64 3)

      (define x64-word-true i64 11)

      (define x64-word-nil i64 19)

      (define x64-fixnum-max i64 1152921504606846975)

      "The failures the runtime says, by number (kayak-kcrt's `kc_fail`)."
      (define x64-fail-not-a-char i64 1)

      (define x64-fail-past-fixnum i64 2)

      (define x64-fail-division i64 3)

      (define x64-fail-not-a-pair i64 4)

      (define x64-fail-heap i64 5)

      (define x64-fail-stack i64 8)

      (define x64-constant-of (subr kfx (sexp) i64)
        (lambda (t)
          "A constant term's value, as a word of Fixpt's format."
          (let ((h (term-head t)) (n (term-number t)))
            (cond ((string=? h "int") (i64* n 8))
                  ((string=? h "bool") (x64-immediate n 0))
                  ((string=? h "nil") (x64-immediate 2 0))
                  ((string=? h "unit") (x64-immediate 3 0))
                  ((string=? h "char") (x64-immediate 8 n))
                  (else (begin (error (string-append "kc: the native back end has no constant " h)) 0))))))

      "Code so far: its lines, the newest first; the next label's number; how
       many of the frame's slots it uses; and the failures' calls, kept out of
       the line, after the code's `ret` (the newest first)."
      (define-datatype x64-code (x64-code (listof string acyclic) i64 i64 (listof string acyclic) string))

      (define x64-emit (subr kfx (x64-code string) x64-code)
        (lambda (c line) (tagcase c (x64-code (ls n k fs px) (x64-code (cons (string-append "    " (string-append line "\n")) ls) n k fs px)))))

      "A cell's store (C451): through the code area's writable view, the
       address `%rcx` made less the state's code distance (Fixpt's `delta`,
       the state in `%r15`), as kc's code runs from the area's executable
       view in process; a built program's state says a distance of no
       pages, so the same bytes store to the cell itself there."
      (define x64-cell-stored (subr kfx (string string) string)
        (lambda (r cell)
          (string-list-append (list "    leaq " cell "(%rip), %rcx\n    subq 208(%r15), %rcx\n    movq " r ", -4(%rcx)\n"))))

      "A function's entry's checks (C451, kc's own convention, the state in
       `%r15` as Fixpt's native convention keeps it), after its frame is
       made: the stack pointer below the state's limit (Fixpt's
       `stack-limit`, 16) a failure, `stack overflow`; then a unit of the
       state's fuel (24) taken, and none left (a borrow) the state's `poll`
       routine (560) called, which gives the next slice, as Fixpt's code
       does on entry. Each call out of the line (`x64-entry-calls`), after
       the function's code."
      (define x64-entry-checks (subr kfx (string) string)
        (lambda (sym)
          (string-list-append (list "    cmpq 16(%r15), %rsp\n    jb .Lck_" sym "_deep\n    subq $1, 24(%r15)\n    jb .Lck_" sym "_poll\n.Lck_" sym "_go:\n"))))

      (define x64-entry-calls (subr kfx (string) string)
        (lambda (sym)
          (string-list-append (list ".Lck_" sym "_deep:\n    movl $" (i64->string x64-fail-stack) ", %edi\n    call kc_fail\n"
                                    ".Lck_" sym "_poll:\n    call *560(%r15)\n    jmp .Lck_" sym "_go\n"))))

      "Lines already made, as they are, after the code so far."
      (define x64-emit-lines (subr kfx (x64-code string) x64-code)
        (lambda (c text) (tagcase c (x64-code (ls n k fs px) (x64-code (cons text ls) n k fs px)))))

      (define x64-emit-label (subr kfx (x64-code string) x64-code)
        (lambda (c l) (tagcase c (x64-code (ls n k fs px) (x64-code (cons (string-append l ":\n") ls) n k fs px)))))

      (define x64-fresh-label (subr kfx (x64-code) i64) (lambda (c) (tagcase c (x64-code (ls n k fs px) n))))

      (define x64-labelled (subr kfx (x64-code) x64-code) (lambda (c) (tagcase c (x64-code (ls n k fs px) (x64-code ls (i64+ n 1) k fs px)))))

      (define x64-label (subr kfx (x64-code string i64) string)
        (lambda (c what n) (tagcase c (x64-code (ls k slots fs px) (string-list-append (list ".L" px "_" what (i64->string n)))))))

      (define x64-using (subr kfx (x64-code i64) x64-code)
        (lambda (c slots) (tagcase c (x64-code (ls n k fs px) (x64-code ls n (if (i64> slots k) slots k) fs px)))))

      (define x64-slot (subr kfx (i64) string)
        (lambda (i) (string-append (i64->string (i64* 8 i)) "(%rsp)")))

      (define x64-boolean-if (subr kfx (x64-code string) x64-code)
        (lambda (c cc)
          "`%rax` made #t if the flags say `cc`, else #f."
          (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c (string-append "movl $" (string-append (i64->string x64-word-false) ", %eax")))
                              (string-append "movl $" (string-append (i64->string x64-word-true) ", %ecx")))
                    (string-append "cmov" (string-append cc " %rcx, %rax")))))

      "An allocation's check (C453), its bytes' end in `%rdx` made by `lea`
       from `%r12`: past the heap's end, the collector called out of the
       line (`kc_gc_call`, given how many bytes), the values in registers
       pushed first (`pre`) for it to move and popped after (`post`), and
       the check made again."
      (define x64-allocating (subr kfx (x64-code string string string) x64-code)
        (lambda (c lea pre post)
          (let* ((k (x64-fresh-label c)) (again (x64-label c "alloc" k)) (gc (x64-label c "gc" k))
                 (c (x64-labelled c))
                 (c (x64-emit-label c again))
                 (c (x64-emit c lea))
                 (c (x64-emit c "cmpq %r13, %rdx"))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "ja " gc))))
            (tagcase c
              (x64-code (ls n slots fs px)
                (x64-code ls n slots
                          (cons (string-list-append (list gc ":\n" pre "    movq %rdx, %rdi\n    subq %r12, %rdi\n    call kc_gc_call\n" post "    jmp " again "\n")) fs)
                          px))))))

      "A frame's slots zeroed (C453), so that the collector, which reads
       every word of kc's stack, meets no word left by a frame before."
      (define-rec
        (x64-frame-zeroed (subr kfx (i64 i64 (listof string acyclic)) string)
          (lambda (bytes at acc)
            (if (i64>= at bytes)
                (string-list-append (reverse acc))
                (x64-frame-zeroed bytes (i64+ at 8) (cons (string-list-append (list "    movq $0, " (i64->string at) "(%rsp)\n")) acc))))))

      (define x64-failing-if (subr kfx (x64-code string i64) x64-code)
        (lambda (c cc what)
          "A jump, if the flags say `cc`, to the failure `what`, whose call is out
           of the line, after the code's `ret`."
          (let* ((k (x64-fresh-label c)) (bad (x64-label c "fail" k))
                 (c (x64-emit (x64-labelled c) (string-append "j" (string-append cc (string-append " " bad))))))
            (tagcase c
              (x64-code (ls n slots fs px)
                (x64-code ls n slots
                          (cons (string-list-append (list bad ":\n    movl $" (i64->string what) ", %edi\n    call kc_fail\n")) fs)
                          px))))))

      "The bloblet kind a predicate tests for (C448)."
      (define x64-kind-of (subr kfx (string) i64)
        (lambda (n)
          (cond ((string=? n "array?") 32) ((string=? n "ref?") 10) ((string=? n "sum?") 36) ((string=? n "product?") 37)
                ((string=? n "vector?") 3) ((string=? n "bytevector?") 4) ((string=? n "f64?") 5) (else 48))))

      (define x64-comparisons (listof string acyclic) (list "=" "<" "<=" ">" ">=" "char=?" "char<?" "char<=?" "char>?" "char>=?" "eq?" "symbol=?"))

      (define x64-condition (subr kfx (string) string)
        (lambda (n)
          "The condition code of a comparison, its first argument in `%rax`, its
           second in `%rcx`: characters compare as their words do, the code above
           the same low bits."
          (cond ((or (string=? n "=") (string=? n "char=?") (string=? n "eq?") (string=? n "symbol=?")) "e")
                ((or (string=? n "<") (string=? n "char<?")) "l")
                ((or (string=? n "<=") (string=? n "char<=?")) "le")
                ((or (string=? n ">") (string=? n "char>?")) "g")
                (else "ge"))))

      "A global's assembly names: its value's cell, its procedure. A name's
       characters but letters and digits each `_` and its code in hexadecimal,
       so that every name is one the assembler takes and no two are one."
      (define-rec
        (x64-name-chars (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) (listof string acyclic)) (listof string acyclic))
          (lambda (cs acc)
            (if (null? cs)
                acc
                (let ((k (char->i64 (car cs))))
                  (x64-name-chars (cdr cs)
                                  (cons (if (or (and (i64>= k 97) (i64<= k 122)) (and (i64>= k 65) (i64<= k 90)) (and (i64>= k 48) (i64<= k 57)))
                                            (list->string (list (car cs)))
                                            (string-append "_" (string-append (kc-hex k "") "_")))
                                        acc)))))))

      (define x64-name (subr kfx (string) string) (lambda (n) (string-list-append (reverse (x64-name-chars (string-chars n) nil)))))

      (define x64-global-symbol (subr kfx (string) string) (lambda (n) (string-append "kcg_" (x64-name n))))

      (define x64-proc-symbol (subr kfx (string) string) (lambda (n) (string-append "kcp_" (x64-name n))))

      "The registers a call's arguments are given in, in order."
      (define x64-arg-registers (listof string acyclic) (list "%rdi" "%rsi" "%rdx" "%rcx" "%r8" "%r9"))

      "A run's own words (C466, TODO §55 item 1; K8): in the state block
       `%r15` holds, one per run (in process, kayak-jit's, one per thread;
       built, kcrt's one), past kayak's `leave` (656), never in cells of
       the image, which every thread running it would share. By offset:
         664  `kc_prompts`, the innermost prompt's or mark's record (C458)
         672  `kc_run_base`, the run's frame, where `cwcc` ends (C460)
         680  `kc_heap_next`, the heap's next word between calls (C448)
         688  `kc_gc`, the collector's block, 7 words (C453; kcrt-core's
              `gc.rs`): the space, its end, the stack's base, the
              globals' cells' run, the next word, a routine's stack
         744  the entry's stack pointer, for a failure (C452)
         752  arguments past the sixth, 58 words (C464)
       152 words in all (kayak-jit's `state::WORDS_IN_STATE`, kcrt's
       `STATE_WORDS`). The globals' cells stay the image's: a program's
       definitions, made once, what FX-26's processes share.

       Arguments past the sixth (C464): the seventh first, which the callee
       copies into its frame on entry, after its registers'
       (`x64-loaded-args`). Nothing between the caller's stores and that
       copy collects (the entry's checks fail or give fuel, every register
       kept), so the words are no roots; nor does a tail call need room on
       a caller's stack. Larceny's convention, Fixpt's register code's,
       passes them as a list instead, a `cons` each at each call; kc's
       convention is its own. At most `x64-most-args`."
      (define x64-most-args i64 64)
      (define x64-state-args i64 752)

      (define-rec
        (x64-spilled-args (subr kfx (x64-code i64 i64 i64) x64-code)
          (lambda (c si k n)
            "Arguments `k` (from 6) to `n` - 1, from the slots from `si`, stored
             in the state block's words from `x64-state-args`."
            (if (i64>= k n)
                c
                (x64-spilled-args
                  (x64-emit (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot (i64+ si k)) ", %rax")))
                            (string-append "movq %rax, " (string-append (i64->string (i64+ x64-state-args (i64* 8 (i64- k 6)))) "(%r15)")))
                  si (i64+ k 1) n)))))

      (define x64-args-passed (subr kfx (x64-code i64 i64) x64-code)
        (lambda (c si n)
          "The `n` arguments in the slots from `si` where the callee takes them:
           the first six in registers, the rest in the state block's words."
          (x64-moved-args
            (if (i64> n 6)
                (x64-spilled-args c si 6 n)
                c)
            x64-arg-registers si n)))

      (define-rec
        (x64-loaded-args (subr kfx (x64-code i64 i64) x64-code)
          (lambda (c k n)
            "Parameters `k` (from 6) to `n` - 1, from the state block into their slots."
            (if (i64>= k n)
                c
                (x64-loaded-args
                  (x64-emit (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (i64->string (i64+ x64-state-args (i64* 8 (i64- k 6)))) "(%r15), %rax")))
                            (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot k)))
                  (i64+ k 1) n)))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-moved-args (subr kfx (x64-code (listof string acyclic) i64 i64) x64-code)
          (lambda (c regs si n)
            "The `n` arguments in the slots from `si` moved to their registers."
            (if (or (i64<= n 0) (null? regs))
                c
                (x64-moved-args (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot si) (string-append ", " (car regs))))) (cdr regs) (i64+ si 1) (i64- n 1))))))

      "A closure (C412), as Fixpt lays one out (`fixpt-heap`'s `layout.rs`,
       `closure`; `make_closure`): a bloblet of kind 8, its fields from the
       header up its free values, the last first, then its code, the heap's
       stub (none yet, 0), and a trailer, the words back to the header; the
       value its suffix's address, past the trailer, tag 4. Field `k` (from
       1, the trailer) is at `-4 - 8k` from the value: the code at -28, free
       value `i` at `-36 - 8i`. The code is the function's address, aligned
       so that it reads as a fixnum (no code bloblets yet)."
      (define x64-closure-header (subr kfx (i64) i64)
        (lambda (m) (i64+ 70 (i64* (i64+ m 3) 16384))))

      (define x64-closure-trailer (subr kfx (i64) i64)
        (lambda (m) (i64+ 5 (i64* (i64+ m 3) 8))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-stored-free (subr kfx (x64-code (listof i64 acyclic) i64 i64) x64-code)
          (lambda (c slots m j)
            "Free value `i` from slot `slots[i]`, at word `m - i` of the cell."
            (if (null? slots)
                c
                (x64-stored-free (x64-emit (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot (car slots)) ", %rcx")))
                                           (string-append "movq %rcx, " (string-append (i64->string (i64* 8 (i64- m j))) "(%r12)")))
                                 (cdr slots) m (i64+ j 1))))))

      (define x64-emit-closure (subr kfx (x64-code string (listof i64 acyclic)) x64-code)
        (lambda (c code slots)
          "A closure of `code` over the values in `slots`, in `%rax`."
          (let* ((m (size slots)) (bytes (i64* 8 (i64+ m 4)))
                 (c (x64-allocating c (string-append "leaq " (string-append (i64->string bytes) "(%r12), %rdx")) "" ""))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movabsq $" (string-append (i64->string (x64-closure-header m)) ", %rcx"))))
                 (c (x64-emit c "movq %rcx, 0(%r12)"))
                 (c (x64-stored-free c slots m 0))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "leaq " (string-append code "(%rip), %rcx"))))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rcx, " (string-append (i64->string (i64* 8 (i64+ m 1))) "(%r12)"))))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq $0, " (string-append (i64->string (i64* 8 (i64+ m 2))) "(%r12)"))))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq $" (string-append (i64->string (x64-closure-trailer m)) (string-append ", " (string-append (i64->string (i64* 8 (i64+ m 3))) "(%r12)"))))))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "leaq " (string-append (i64->string (i64+ bytes 4)) "(%r12), %rax")))))
            (x64-emit c "movq %rdx, %r12"))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-loaded-free (subr kfx (x64-code i64 i64 i64) x64-code)
          (lambda (c i m si)
            "A lambda's free values, from its closure in `%r10`, each to its slot."
            (if (i64>= i m)
                c
                (x64-loaded-free (x64-emit (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (i64->string (i64- -36 (i64* 8 i))) "(%r10), %rax")))
                                           (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot (i64+ si i))))
                                 (i64+ i 1) m si)))))

      "A string as Fixpt lays one out (C421; `fixpt-heap`'s `make_string`): a
       header of kind 1, its words all suffix; its length; its code points,
       two a word, the first in the low half. In `.rodata`, from `label`,
       the string's value `label` + 4 (its suffix, tag 4)."
      (define-rec
        (x64-points (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) (listof string acyclic)) (listof string acyclic))
          (lambda (cs acc)
            (cond ((null? cs) (reverse acc))
                  ((null? (cdr cs)) (reverse (cons (string-append "    .quad " (string-append (i64->string (char->i64 (car cs))) "\n")) acc)))
                  (else (x64-points (cdr (cdr cs))
                                    (cons (string-list-append (list "    .quad " (i64->string (i64+ (char->i64 (car cs)) (i64* (char->i64 (second-char cs)) 4294967296))) "\n")) acc)))))))

      (define second-char (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic)) char) (lambda (cs) (car (cdr cs))))

      (define x64-string-data (subr kfx (string string) string)
        (lambda (label text)
          (let* ((cs (string-chars text)) (n (size cs)) (words (i64+ 1 (i64-quotient (i64+ n 1) 2))))
            (string-list-append
              (append (list "    .section .rodata\n    .p2align 3\n    .quad " (i64->string (i64+ 14 (i64* (i64* 8 words) 4294967296))) "\n"
                            label ":\n    .quad " (i64->string n) "\n")
                      (append (x64-points cs nil) (list "    .text\n")))))))

      "A literal's data, out of the line with the failures' calls, and its
       label."
      (define x64-data (subr kfx (x64-code string) x64-code)
        (lambda (c text) (tagcase c (x64-code (ls n k fs px) (x64-code ls n k (cons text fs) px)))))

      (define x64-calling (subr kfx (x64-code string) x64-code)
        (lambda (c f)
          "`%rax`, then `%rcx`, given to the runtime's `f`, its answer in `%rax`."
          (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "movq %rcx, %rsi") (string-append "call " f))))

      "An array's element (C422; Fixpt's `make-array` and `array-ref`):
       `%rax` the array, `%rcx` the index, a fixnum, checked against the
       length (the trailer's distance, less one), unsigned, so that one
       below 0 is past it; `%rsi` made the address from which the element
       is at -20 (the value's tag 4, then the trailer and the element's
       place counted back from it, `-4 - 8 (i + 2)`)."
      (define x64-array-index (subr kfx (x64-code) x64-code)
        (lambda (c)
          (let* ((k (x64-fresh-label c)) (bad (x64-label c "fail" k))
                 (c (x64-labelled c))
                 (c (x64-emit c "sarq $3, %rcx"))
                 (c (x64-emit c "movq -12(%rax), %rsi"))
                 (c (x64-emit c "shrq $3, %rsi"))
                 (c (x64-emit c "decq %rsi"))
                 (c (x64-emit c "cmpq %rsi, %rcx"))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "jae " bad)))
                 (c (tagcase c (x64-code (ls n slots fs px)
                                 (x64-code ls n slots (cons (string-list-append (list bad ":\n    movq %rsi, %rdi\n    call kc_array_index_fail\n")) fs) px))))
                 (c (x64-emit c "movq %rcx, %rsi"))
                 (c (x64-emit c "shlq $3, %rsi"))
                 (c (x64-emit c "negq %rsi")))
            (x64-emit c "addq %rax, %rsi"))))

      "A symbol named `name` in `%rax` (C421): interned by the runtime the
       first time it is met, and kept in a cell of its name's, common to every
       object that names it."
      (define x64-emit-symbol (subr kfx (x64-code string) x64-code)
        (lambda (c name)
          (let* ((k (x64-fresh-label c)) (l (x64-label c "str" k)) (done (x64-label c "sym" k)) (c (x64-labelled c))
                 (cell (string-append "kcy_" (x64-name name)))
                 (c (x64-data c (string-append (x64-string-data l name) (string-append "    .comm " (string-append cell ",8,8\n")))))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append cell "(%rip), %rax"))))
                 (c (x64-emit c "testq %rax, %rax"))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "jne " done)))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "leaq " (string-append l "+4(%rip), %rdi"))))
                 (c (x64-emit c "call kc_intern"))
                 (c (x64-emit-lines c (x64-cell-stored "%rax" cell))))
            (x64-emit-label c done))))

      "A bloblet of kind `kind` of the `n` values in the slots from `si`, in
       order, and a trailer, from the heap, in `%rax` (C423; Fixpt's sums,
       kind 36, its tag and its payload; products, kind 37, its fields):
       value `i` the field `i + 2` back from the value, as an array's
       element is."
      (define-rec
        (x64-stored-values (subr kfx (x64-code i64 i64 i64) x64-code)
          (lambda (c si i n)
            (if (i64>= i n)
                c
                (x64-stored-values (x64-emit (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot (i64+ si i)) ", %rcx")))
                                             (string-append "movq %rcx, " (string-append (i64->string (i64* 8 (i64- n i))) "(%r12)")))
                                   si (i64+ i 1) n)))))

      (define x64-emit-bloblet (subr kfx (x64-code i64 i64 i64) x64-code)
        (lambda (c kind si n)
          (let* ((bytes (i64* 8 (i64+ n 2)))
                 (c (x64-allocating c (string-append "leaq " (string-append (i64->string bytes) "(%r12), %rdx")) "" ""))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movabsq $" (string-append (i64->string (i64+ (i64+ 6 (i64* kind 8)) (i64* (i64+ n 1) 16384))) ", %rcx"))))
                 (c (x64-emit c "movq %rcx, 0(%r12)"))
                 (c (x64-stored-values c si 0 n))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq $" (string-append (i64->string (i64+ 5 (i64* (i64+ n 1) 8))) (string-append ", " (string-append (i64->string (i64* 8 (i64+ n 1))) "(%r12)"))))))
                 (c (x64-emit c (string-append "leaq " (string-append (i64->string (i64+ bytes 4)) "(%r12), %rax")))))
            (x64-emit c "movq %rdx, %r12"))))

      "Where each variable is: its binder's number and its slot."
      (define-datatype x64-at (x64-at i64 i64))

      (define-rec
        (x64-slot-of (subr kfx (i64 (listof x64-at acyclic)) i64)
          (lambda (k env)
            (cond ((null? env) (the i64 -1))
                  ((tagcase (car env) (x64-at (j s) (i64= j k))) (tagcase (car env) (x64-at (j s) s)))
                  (else (x64-slot-of k (cdr env)))))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-params-at (subr kfx (sexps i64 (listof x64-at acyclic)) (listof x64-at acyclic))
          (lambda (ps i env)
            (if (null? ps) env
                (x64-params-at (cdr ps) (i64+ i 1) (cons (x64-at (tagcase (car (items (car ps))) (num (k f p) k) (else other -1)) i) env))))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-stored-params (subr kfx (x64-code (listof string acyclic) i64 i64) x64-code)
          (lambda (c regs i n)
            (if (or (i64>= i n) (null? regs)) c
                (x64-stored-params (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (car regs) (string-append ", " (x64-slot i))))) (cdr regs) (i64+ i 1) n)))))

      (define term-at-number (subr kfx (sexp i64) i64)
        (lambda (t i) (tagcase (car (reverse (items t))) (num (k f p) k) (else other 0))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-fields-bound (subr kfx (x64-code i64 i64 i64) x64-code)
          (lambda (c si j m)
            "A product's fields, from `%rdx`, field `j` (from 1) at `-12 - 8j`,
             each to its slot from `si`."
            (if (i64> j m)
                c
                (x64-fields-bound (x64-emit (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (i64->string (i64- -12 (i64* 8 j))) "(%rdx), %rsi")))
                                            (string-append "movq %rsi, " (x64-slot si)))
                                  (i64+ si 1) (i64+ j 1) m)))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-zeroed (subr kfx (x64-code i64 i64) x64-code)
          (lambda (c si n) (if (i64<= n 0) c (x64-zeroed (x64-emit c (string-append "movq $0, " (x64-slot si))) (i64+ si 1) (i64- n 1))))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-free-patched (subr kfx (x64-code sexps i64 i64 (listof i64 acyclic) (listof x64-at acyclic)) x64-code)
          (lambda (c fv j slot group env)
            "Of the closure in slot `slot`, each free value `j` on that is one of
             the group's binders (their numbers `group`) set from its slot."
            (if (null? fv)
                c
                (let ((k (tagcase (car (items (car fv))) (num (n f p) n) (else other (the i64 -1)))))
                  (x64-free-patched
                    (if (i64-in? k group)
                        (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot (x64-slot-of k env)) ", %rcx")))
                                            (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot slot) ", %rax")))
                                  (string-append "movq %rcx, " (string-append (i64->string (i64- -36 (i64* 8 j))) "(%rax)")))
                        c)
                    (cdr fv) (i64+ j 1) slot group env))))))

      (define-rec
        (i64-in? (subr kfx (i64 (listof i64 acyclic)) bool)
          (lambda (k ks) (cond ((null? ks) #f) ((i64= (car ks) k) #t) (else (i64-in? k (cdr ks)))))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-letrec-patched (subr kfx (x64-code sexps i64 i64 sexps (listof x64-at acyclic)) x64-code)
          (lambda (c vs si i bs env)
            (if (null? vs)
                c
                (x64-letrec-patched
                  (if (string=? (term-head (car vs)) "lambda")
                      (x64-free-patched c (lambda-free (car vs)) 0 (i64+ si i)
                                        (map (lambda ((b sexp)) (tagcase (car (items b)) (num (n f p) n) (else other (the i64 -1)))) bs) env)
                      c)
                  (cdr vs) si (i64+ i 1) bs env)))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-but-last (subr kfx (sexps) sexps)
          (lambda (xs) (if (or (null? xs) (null? (cdr xs))) nil (cons (car xs) (x64-but-last (cdr xs)))))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-emit-expr (subr kfx (x64-code sexp i64 (listof x64-at acyclic)) x64-code)
          (lambda (c t si env)
            "Code that leaves `t`'s value in `%rax`, using the frame's slots from
             `si`, its variables where `env` says."
            (let ((h (term-head t)))
              (cond ((and (string=? h "prim") (i64< (size (prim-args t)) 3) (not (string=? (prim-name t) "new")))
                     (let ((args (prim-args t)))
                       (if (null? (cdr args))
                           (x64-emit-unary (x64-emit-expr c (car args) si env) (prim-name t))
                           ;; The first in slot `si` while the second is made; then the
                           ;; first in `%rax`, the second in `%rcx`.
                           (let* ((c (x64-emit-expr c (car args) si env))
                                  (c (x64-using (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot si))) (i64+ si 1)))
                                  (c (x64-emit-expr c (second args) (i64+ si 1) env))
                                  (c (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rcx"))
                                  (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot si) ", %rax")))))
                             (x64-emit-binary c (prim-name t))))))
                    ((string=? h "var") (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot (x64-slot-of (var-number t) env)) ", %rax"))))
                    ((string=? h "gvar") (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-global-symbol (item-name t)) "(%rip), %rax"))))
                    ((string=? h "call")
                     ;; Each argument made into a slot of its own, then moved to its
                     ;; register, and the procedure called (C407).
                     (let* ((args (call-args t)) (n (size args)))
                       (if (i64> n x64-most-args)
                           (begin (not-yet "" "a call of more than 64 arguments") c)
                           (let* ((c (x64-emit-args c args si env))
                                  (c (x64-args-passed c si n)))
                             (x64-emit c (string-append "call " (x64-proc-symbol (call-name t))))))))
                    ((string=? h "if")
                     ;; The test, a bool: #f's word to the else, all else to the then (C405).
                     (let* ((ps (if-parts t))
                            (k (x64-fresh-label c)) (no (x64-label c "else" k)) (past (x64-label c "fi" k))
                            (c (x64-labelled c))
                            (c (x64-emit-expr c (car ps) si env))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "cmpq $" (string-append (i64->string x64-word-false) ", %rax"))))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "je " no)))
                            (c (x64-emit-expr c (second ps) si env))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "jmp " past)))
                            (c (x64-emit-label c no))
                            (c (x64-emit-expr c (third ps) si env)))
                       (x64-emit-label c past)))
                    ((string=? h "string")
                     ;; Its data in `.rodata`; its value its suffix's address, tag 4.
                     (let* ((k (x64-fresh-label c)) (l (x64-label c "str" k)) (c (x64-labelled c))
                            (c (x64-data c (x64-string-data l (term-text t)))))
                       (x64-emit c (string-append "leaq " (string-append l "+4(%rip), %rax")))))
                    ((string=? h "symbol") (x64-emit-symbol c (term-text t)))
                    ;; Products, sums, `extract`, `tagcase` (C423).
                    ((string=? h "product")
                     (let* ((args (cdr (items t))) (c (x64-emit-args c args si env)))
                       (x64-emit-bloblet c 37 si (size args))))
                    ((string=? h "extract")
                     (let ((c (x64-emit-expr c (second (items t)) si env)))
                       (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (i64->string (i64- -12 (i64* 8 (term-at-number t 2)))) "(%rax), %rax")))))
                    ((string=? h "sum")
                     ;; Its payload into the slot after the tag's, the tag (a
                     ;; symbol, interned) into its own; then the two.
                     (let* ((c (x64-emit-expr c (third (items t)) (i64+ si 1) env))
                            (c (x64-using (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot (i64+ si 1)))) (i64+ si 2)))
                            (c (x64-emit-symbol c (term-text t)))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot si)))))
                       (x64-emit-bloblet c 36 si 2)))
                    ((string=? h "tagcase") (x64-emit-tagcase c t si env ""))
                    ((string=? h "letrec") (x64-emit-letrec c t si env ""))
                    ((and (string=? h "prim") (string=? (prim-name t) "new"))
                     ;; A ref, Fixpt's box (kind 10): its one field the value (C424).
                     (let* ((c (x64-emit-expr c (car (prim-args t)) si env))
                            (c (x64-using (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot si))) (i64+ si 1))))
                       (x64-emit-bloblet c 10 si 1)))
                    ((and (string=? h "prim") (string=? (prim-name t) "array-set!"))
                     ;; The array, the index and the value into slots, then into
                     ;; `%rax`, `%rcx`, `%rdx`; the index checked as `array-ref`'s
                     ;; is; unit (C422).
                     (let* ((args (prim-args t))
                            (c (x64-emit-args c args si env))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot si) ", %rax"))))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot (i64+ si 1)) ", %rcx"))))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot (i64+ si 2)) ", %rdx"))))
                            (c (x64-array-index c)))
                       (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rdx, -20(%rsi)") (string-append "movq $" (string-append (i64->string (x64-constant-of (car (read-all "(unit)" "l0" 1)))) ", %rax")))))
                    ((and (string=? h "prim") (string=? (prim-name t) "with-mark"))
                     ;; A mark (C460): the key, the value and the thunk to `kc_with_mark`.
                     (let* ((c (x64-emit-args c (prim-args t) si env))
                            (c (x64-moved-args c x64-arg-registers si 3)))
                       (x64-emit c "call kc_with_mark")))
                    ((and (string=? h "prim") (i64= (size (prim-args t)) 3))
                     ;; `substring`: its arguments into slots, then given to the runtime.
                     (let* ((args (prim-args t))
                            (c (x64-emit-args c args si env))
                            (c (x64-moved-args c x64-arg-registers si 3)))
                       (x64-emit c "call kc_substring")))
                    ((string=? h "prompt") (x64-emit-prompt c t si env))
                    ((string=? h "lambda") (x64-emit-lambda c t env))
                    ((string=? h "gproc") (x64-emit-closure c (x64-proc-symbol (item-name t)) nil))
                    ((string=? h "app")
                     ;; The procedure into slot `si`, its arguments after it, then its
                     ;; code called, the closure in `%r10` (C412).
                     (let* ((args (app-args t)) (n (size args)))
                       (if (i64> n x64-most-args)
                           (begin (not-yet "" "a call of more than 64 arguments") c)
                           (let* ((c (x64-emit-expr c (app-fn t) si env))
                                  (c (x64-using (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot si))) (i64+ si 1)))
                                  (c (x64-emit-args c args (i64+ si 1) env))
                                  (c (x64-args-passed c (i64+ si 1) n))
                                  (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot si) ", %r10")))))
                             (x64-emit c "call *-28(%r10)")))))
                    ((string=? h "let") (x64-emit-let c (let-bindings t) (let-body t) si env env ""))
                    ((string=? h "seq") (x64-emit-seq c (seq-terms t) si env))
                    (else (x64-emit c (string-append "movabsq $" (string-append (i64->string (x64-constant-of t)) ", %rax"))))))))

        (x64-emit-lambda (subr kfx (x64-code sexp (listof x64-at acyclic)) x64-code)
          (lambda (c t env)
            "A lambda (C412): its function, out of the line, after the code's
             `ret` with the failures' calls, its parameters' and free values'
             slots first; and here, a closure of it over the free values."
            (let* ((ps (lambda-params t)) (n (size ps)) (fv (lambda-free t)) (m (size fv)))
              (if (i64> n x64-most-args)
                  (begin (not-yet "" "a lambda of more than 64 parameters") c)
                  (tagcase c
                    (x64-code (ls k slots fs px)
                      (let* ((sym (string-list-append (list "kcl_" px "_" (i64->string (term-number t)))))
                             (fr (x64-label c "frame" k))
                             (inner (x64-using (x64-code nil (i64+ k 1) 0 nil px) (i64+ n m)))
                             (inner (x64-loaded-args (x64-stored-params inner x64-arg-registers 0 n) 6 n))
                             (inner (x64-loaded-free inner 0 m n))
                             (env2 (x64-params-at fv n (x64-params-at ps 0 nil)))
                             (inner (x64-emit-tail inner (item-body t) (i64+ n m) env2 fr)))
                        (tagcase inner
                          (x64-code (ls2 k2 slots2 fs2 px2)
                            (let ((frame (x64-frame-of-call slots2)))
                              (x64-emit-closure
                                (x64-code ls k2 slots
                                          (cons (string-list-append
                                                  (append (list "    .p2align 4\n" sym ":\n    subq $" fr ", %rsp\n" (x64-entry-checks sym) (x64-frame-zeroed frame 0 nil))
                                                          (append (reverse ls2)
                                                                  (append (reverse fs2)
                                                                          (list (x64-entry-calls sym) "    .set " fr ", " (i64->string frame) "\n")))))
                                                fs)
                                          px)
                                sym
                                (map (lambda ((v sexp)) (x64-slot-of (tagcase (car (items v)) (num (j f p) j) (else other -1)) env)) fv))))))))))))

        (x64-emit-prompt (subr kfx (x64-code sexp i64 (listof x64-at acyclic)) x64-code)
          (lambda (c t si env)
            "A prompt (C458), as Fixpt's native convention has one, a frame of a
             known kind (`docs/research/native-conventions.md`): its tag, then
             its handler, made, then its body, a closure of no parameters
             (C459); then a record of it in the frame's slots from `si` (the
             prompt before it, the tag, the stack pointer, and where its
             handler's call is), the innermost prompt `kc_prompts` holds; then
             the body called, so that all it does is above this frame, the
             return to it just below the record's stack pointer, where a
             capture's segment ends (`kc_capture`); and the record taken off. An
             abort (`kc_abort`) finds the record of its tag's innermost prompt,
             takes it and those inside it off, makes the stack pointer the
             record's and goes to the handler's call, its value in `%rax`: the
             handler called on it, in the prompt's continuation. Each word of
             the record a value, a stack address or a code address, as the
             collector's scan of the stack wants."
            (let* ((xs (items t)) (k (x64-fresh-label c))
                   (handler (x64-label c "abort" k)) (past (x64-label c "prompted" k))
                   (c (x64-labelled c))
                   (c (x64-using c (i64+ si 6)))
                   (c (x64-emit-expr c (second xs) (i64+ si 6) env))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot (i64+ si 1)))))
                   (c (x64-emit-expr c (third xs) (i64+ si 6) env))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot (i64+ si 4)))))
                   (c (x64-emit-expr c (fourth xs) (i64+ si 6) env))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot (i64+ si 5)))))
                   (c (x64-emit c "movq 664(%r15), %rdx"))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rdx, " (x64-slot si))))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rsp, " (x64-slot (i64+ si 2)))))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "leaq " (string-append handler "(%rip), %rdx"))))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rdx, " (x64-slot (i64+ si 3)))))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "leaq " (string-append (x64-slot si) ", %rdx"))))
                   (c (x64-emit-lines c "    movq %rdx, 664(%r15)\n"))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot (i64+ si 5)) ", %r10"))))
                   (c (x64-emit c "call *-28(%r10)"))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot si) ", %rdx"))))
                   (c (x64-emit-lines c "    movq %rdx, 664(%r15)\n"))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "jmp " past)))
                   (c (x64-emit-label c handler))
                   (c (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi"))
                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot (i64+ si 4)) ", %r10"))))
                   (c (x64-emit c "call *-28(%r10)")))
              (x64-emit-label c past))))

        (x64-emit-tail (subr kfx (x64-code sexp i64 (listof x64-at acyclic) string) x64-code)
          (lambda (c t si env fr)
            "Code for `t` in tail position (C413), of a function whose frame is
             `fr` bytes: its value returned, or, a call, the frame given back and
             the callee jumped to, so that it returns to this one's caller; its
             arguments are in registers, so no frame of the caller's is written."
            (let ((h (term-head t)))
              (cond ((string=? h "if")
                     (let* ((ps (if-parts t))
                            (k (x64-fresh-label c)) (no (x64-label c "else" k))
                            (c (x64-labelled c))
                            (c (x64-emit-expr c (car ps) si env))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "cmpq $" (string-append (i64->string x64-word-false) ", %rax"))))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "je " no)))
                            (c (x64-emit-tail c (second ps) si env fr))
                            (c (x64-emit-label c no)))
                       (x64-emit-tail c (third ps) si env fr)))
                    ((string=? h "let") (x64-emit-let c (let-bindings t) (let-body t) si env env fr))
                    ((string=? h "tagcase") (x64-emit-tagcase c t si env fr))
                    ((string=? h "letrec") (x64-emit-letrec c t si env fr))
                    ((string=? h "seq")
                     (let ((ts (seq-terms t)))
                       (x64-emit-tail (x64-emit-seq c (x64-but-last ts) si env) (car (reverse ts)) si env fr)))
                    ((and (string=? h "call") (i64<= (size (call-args t)) x64-most-args))
                     (let* ((args (call-args t)) (n (size args))
                            (c (x64-emit-args c args si env))
                            (c (x64-args-passed c si n))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "addq $" (string-append fr ", %rsp")))))
                       (x64-emit c (string-append "jmp " (x64-proc-symbol (call-name t))))))
                    ;; A mark in tail position (C460): this frame given back first,
                    ;; so that a mark of the key the return is to is replaced.
                    ((and (string=? h "prim") (string=? (prim-name t) "with-mark"))
                     (let* ((c (x64-emit-args c (prim-args t) si env))
                            (c (x64-moved-args c x64-arg-registers si 3))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "addq $" (string-append fr ", %rsp")))))
                       (x64-emit c "jmp kc_with_mark")))
                    ((and (string=? h "app") (i64<= (size (app-args t)) x64-most-args))
                     (let* ((args (app-args t)) (n (size args))
                            (c (x64-emit-expr c (app-fn t) si env))
                            (c (x64-using (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot si))) (i64+ si 1)))
                            (c (x64-emit-args c args (i64+ si 1) env))
                            (c (x64-args-passed c (i64+ si 1) n))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot si) ", %r10"))))
                            (c (x64-emit c (string-append "addq $" (string-append fr ", %rsp")))))
                       (x64-emit c "jmp *-28(%r10)")))
                    (else
                     (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit-expr c t si env) (string-append "addq $" (string-append fr ", %rsp"))) "ret"))))))

        (x64-emit-letrec (subr kfx (x64-code sexp i64 (listof x64-at acyclic) string) x64-code)
          (lambda (c t si env fr)
            "A `letrec` (C426): its binders' slots from `si`, 0 first; each value,
             a lambda, made into its binder's slot, its free values as the slots
             are then; then each closure's free values that are the group's
             binders patched from their slots, now each made (Ghuloum's way);
             then the body, in tail position if `fr` is given."
            (let* ((bs (letrec-binders t)) (n (size bs))
                   (env2 (x64-params-at bs si env))
                   (c (x64-using c (i64+ si n)))
                   (c (x64-zeroed c si n))
                   (c (x64-letrec-values c (letrec-values t) si (i64+ si n) env2))
                   (c (x64-letrec-patched c (letrec-values t) si 0 bs env2)))
              (if (string=? fr "")
                  (x64-emit-expr c (car (reverse (items t))) (i64+ si n) env2)
                  (x64-emit-tail c (car (reverse (items t))) (i64+ si n) env2 fr)))))

        (x64-letrec-values (subr kfx (x64-code sexps i64 i64 (listof x64-at acyclic)) x64-code)
          (lambda (c vs at si env)
            (if (null? vs)
                c
                (let ((c (x64-emit-expr c (car vs) si env)))
                  (x64-letrec-values (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot at))) (cdr vs) (i64+ at 1) si env)))))

        (x64-emit-tagcase (subr kfx (x64-code sexp i64 (listof x64-at acyclic) string) x64-code)
          (lambda (c t si env fr)
            "A `tagcase` (C423): the sum into slot `si`; each arm, in turn, its
             tag's symbol compared with the sum's (field 2, at -20); the first
             that is the same binds its payload (field 3, at -28), whole or its
             product's fields, or, `else`, the sum, in the slots after, and its
             body is the `tagcase`'s, in tail position if `fr`, its function's
             frame, is given. No arm: none can be, the checker found."
            (let* ((k (x64-fresh-label c)) (past (x64-label c "esac" k)) (c (x64-labelled c))
                   (c (x64-emit-expr c (second (items t)) si env))
                   (c (x64-using (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot si))) (i64+ si 1)))
                   (c (x64-emit-arms c (tagcase-arms t) si env fr past))
                   (c (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movl $7, %edi") "call kc_fail")))
              (if (string=? fr "") (x64-emit-label c past) c))))

        (x64-emit-arms (subr kfx (x64-code sexps i64 (listof x64-at acyclic) string string) x64-code)
          (lambda (c arms si env fr past)
            (if (null? arms)
                c
                (let* ((a (items (car arms)))
                       (kind (tagcase (car a) (sym (n f p) n) (else other "")))
                       (k (x64-fresh-label c)) (next (x64-label c "arm" k)) (c (x64-labelled c))
                       (c (if (string=? kind "else")
                              c
                              (let* ((c (x64-emit-symbol c (tagcase (second a) (str (s f p) s) (else other ""))))
                                     (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot si) ", %rcx"))))
                                     (c (x64-emit c "cmpq -20(%rcx), %rax")))
                                (x64-emit c (string-append "jne " next)))))
                       (binders (cond ((string=? kind "else") (list (second a)))
                                      ((string=? kind "whole") (list (third a)))
                                      (else (items (third a)))))
                       (body (car (reverse a)))
                       (c (x64-emit c (string-append "movq " (string-append (x64-slot si) ", %rcx"))))
                       (c (cond ((string=? kind "else") (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rcx, " (x64-slot (i64+ si 1)))))
                                ((string=? kind "whole") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq -28(%rcx), %rdx") (string-append "movq %rdx, " (x64-slot (i64+ si 1)))))
                                (else (x64-fields-bound (x64-emit c "movq -28(%rcx), %rdx") (i64+ si 1) 1 (size binders)))))
                       (n (size binders))
                       (c (x64-using c (i64+ (i64+ si 1) n)))
                       (env2 (x64-params-at binders (i64+ si 1) env))
                       (c (if (string=? fr "")
                              (x64-emit (x64-emit-expr c body (i64+ (i64+ si 1) n) env2) (string-append "jmp " past))
                              (x64-emit-tail c body (i64+ (i64+ si 1) n) env2 fr)))
                       (c (x64-emit-label c next)))
                  (x64-emit-arms c (cdr arms) si env fr past)))))

        (x64-emit-let (subr kfx (x64-code sexps sexp i64 (listof x64-at acyclic) (listof x64-at acyclic) string) x64-code)
          (lambda (c bs body si env inner fr)
            "Each binding's value made where the `let` is (`env`), into a slot of
             its own; then the body, the binders in scope (`inner`) (C404), in
             tail position if `fr`, its function's frame, is given (C413)."
            (if (null? bs)
                (if (string=? fr "") (x64-emit-expr c body si inner) (x64-emit-tail c body si inner fr))
                (let* ((b (items (car bs)))
                       (k (tagcase (car b) (num (n f p) n) (else other (the i64 -1))))
                       (c (x64-emit-expr c (third b) si env))
                       (c (x64-using (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot si))) (i64+ si 1))))
                  (x64-emit-let c (cdr bs) body (i64+ si 1) env (cons (x64-at k si) inner) fr)))))

        (x64-emit-args (subr kfx (x64-code sexps i64 (listof x64-at acyclic)) x64-code)
          (lambda (c args si env)
            "Each argument made into a slot of its own, from `si`."
            (if (null? args)
                c
                (let* ((c (x64-emit-expr c (car args) si env))
                       (c (x64-using (x64-emit c (string-append "movq %rax, " (x64-slot si))) (i64+ si 1))))
                  (x64-emit-args c (cdr args) (i64+ si 1) env)))))

        (x64-emit-seq (subr kfx (x64-code sexps i64 (listof x64-at acyclic)) x64-code)
          (lambda (c ts si env)
            "Each in turn, the last's value kept."
            (if (null? ts) c (x64-emit-seq (x64-emit-expr c (car ts) si env) (cdr ts) si env))))

        (x64-emit-unary (subr kfx (x64-code string) x64-code)
          (lambda (c n)
            "Code that makes `%rax`, the argument, the primitive `n`'s value."
            (cond ((string=? n "not") (x64-boolean-if (x64-emit c (string-append "cmpq $" (string-append (i64->string x64-word-false) ", %rax"))) "e"))
                  ((string=? n "null?") (x64-boolean-if (x64-emit c (string-append "cmpq $" (string-append (i64->string x64-word-nil) ", %rax"))) "e"))
                  ((string=? n "zero?") (x64-boolean-if (x64-emit c "testq %rax, %rax") "e"))
                  ;; (c << 8 | 67) >> 5 is c << 3 | 2; the tag bits cleared, a fixnum.
                  ((string=? n "char->integer") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "shrq $5, %rax") "andq $-8, %rax"))
                  ((string=? n "integer->char")
                   ;; A Unicode scalar value: 0 to 0x10ffff, but not 0xd800 to 0xdfff.
                   (let* ((c (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "sarq $3, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "cmpq $1114111, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-failing-if c "a" x64-fail-not-a-char))
                          (c (x64-emit c "leaq -55296(%rdx), %rcx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "cmpq $2047, %rcx"))
                          (c (x64-failing-if c "be" x64-fail-not-a-char))
                          (c (x64-emit c "shlq $8, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "orq $67, %rdx")))
                     (x64-emit c "movq %rdx, %rax")))
                  ;; A pair is its cell's address, tag 1: its car at -1 from the
                  ;; value, its cdr at 7 (C406).
                  ((or (string=? n "car") (string=? n "cdr"))
                   (let* ((c (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "andq $7, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "cmpq $1, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-failing-if c "ne" x64-fail-not-a-pair)))
                     (x64-emit c (if (string=? n "car") "movq -1(%rax), %rax" "movq 7(%rax), %rax"))))
                  ((string=? n "pair?")
                   (x64-boolean-if (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdx") "andq $7, %rdx") "cmpq $1, %rdx") "e"))
                  ;; A string's length is its first word, at its suffix (C421).
                  ((string=? n "string-length") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq -4(%rax), %rax") "shlq $3, %rax"))
                  ((string=? n "symbol->string") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_symbol_to_string"))
                  ;; A ref's value, its field 2 back (C424).
                  ((string=? n "get") (x64-emit c "movq -20(%rax), %rax"))
                  ;; Its fields less the trailer, from the trailer's distance (C422).
                  ((string=? n "array-length") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq -12(%rax), %rax") "subq $13, %rax"))
                  ((string=? n "string->symbol") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_intern"))
                  ;; A whole continuation's capture (C460): to the run's frame.
                  ((string=? n "cwcc")
                   (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "movq 672(%r15), %rsi") "movl $32, %edx") "call kc_capture"))
                  ;; A key's marks, innermost first (C460).
                  ((string=? n "current-marks")
                   (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "movq 664(%r15), %rsi") "call kc_current_marks"))
                  ;; Lists and numbers (C462): a list reversed, a number's
                  ;; digits, made in the heap by kcrt (`x64-heap-routine`).
                  ((string=? n "reverse") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_reverse"))
                  ((string=? n "int->string") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_int_to_string"))
                  ;; A list's length, its pairs counted, a fixnum.
                  ((string=? n "length")
                   (let* ((k (x64-fresh-label c)) (loop (x64-label c "len" k)) (done (x64-label c "lend" k))
                          (c (x64-labelled c))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movl $0, %eax"))
                          (c (x64-emit-label c loop))
                          (c (x64-emit c (string-append "cmpq $" (string-append (i64->string x64-word-nil) ", %rdx"))))
                          (c (x64-emit c (string-append "je " done)))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movq %rdx, %rcx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "andq $7, %rcx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "cmpq $1, %rcx"))
                          (c (x64-failing-if c "ne" x64-fail-not-a-pair))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movq 7(%rdx), %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "addq $8, %rax"))
                          (c (x64-emit c (string-append "jmp " loop))))
                     (x64-emit-label c done)))
                  ;; The expander's rest (C470): what is made, in the heap by
                  ;; kcrt; what is asked, kcrt's to say; `error`, the run failed.
                  ((string=? n "char->string") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_char_to_string"))
                  ((string=? n "f64->string") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_f64_to_string"))
                  ((string=? n "datum-list->vector") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_list_to_vector"))
                  ((string=? n "char-whitespace?") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_char_whitespace"))
                  ((string=? n "char-numeric?") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_char_numeric"))
                  ((string=? n "string-hash") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_string_hash"))
                  ((string=? n "symbol-name-hash") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_symbol_hash"))
                  ((string=? n "error") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_error"))
                  ((string=? n "string?") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_is_string"))
                  ((string=? n "symbol?") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_is_symbol"))
                  ;; What a datum is (C447): a fixnum, tag 0; a character, its low
                  ;; byte 67 (kind 8, tag 3); a boolean, 3 or 11; a procedure, a
                  ;; closure, the runtime's to say.
                  ((string=? n "int?") (x64-boolean-if (x64-emit c "testq $7, %rax") "e"))
                  ((string=? n "char?") (x64-boolean-if (x64-emit c "cmpb $67, %al") "e"))
                  ((string=? n "bool?") (x64-boolean-if (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdx") "andq $-9, %rdx") "cmpq $3, %rdx") "e"))
                  ((string=? n "procedure?") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "call kc_is_procedure"))
                  ;; A bloblet of a kind (C448; `fixpt-heap`'s `layout.rs`), the
                  ;; runtime's to say.
                  ((string-member? n (list "array?" "ref?" "sum?" "product?" "vector?" "bytevector?" "keyword?" "f64?"))
                   (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi")
                                       (string-append "movl $" (string-append (i64->string (x64-kind-of n)) ", %esi")))
                             "call kc_is_kind"))
                  (else (begin (error (string-append "kc: the native back end has no primitive " n)) c)))))

        (x64-emit-binary (subr kfx (x64-code string) x64-code)
          (lambda (c n)
            "Code that makes `%rax`, the first argument, and `%rcx`, the second,
             the primitive `n`'s value. A fixnum is its value times 8: a sum or a
             difference of two is the sum's, its overflow the 64-bit one; a
             product, one of them shifted back first."
            (cond ((string-member? n x64-comparisons)
                   (x64-boolean-if (x64-emit c "cmpq %rcx, %rax") (x64-condition n)))
                  ;; An abort to the tag's prompt (C458), never back.
                  ((or (string=? n "abort-current-continuation") (string=? n "escape"))
                   (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "movq %rcx, %rsi") "call kc_abort"))
                  ;; A key's innermost mark, or the default; a continuation's marks (C460).
                  ((string=? n "first-mark") (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "movq %rcx, %rsi") "call kc_first_mark"))
                  ((string=? n "marks-of") (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "movq %rcx, %rsi") "call kc_marks_of"))
                  ;; A capture (C459): the procedure, the tag, and whether once.
                  ((or (string=? n "call-with-composable-continuation") (string=? n "call-with-oneshot-continuation"))
                   (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdi") "movq %rcx, %rsi")
                                       (if (string=? n "call-with-oneshot-continuation") "movl $8, %edx" "movl $0, %edx"))
                             "call kc_capture"))
                  ((string=? n "+") (x64-failing-if (x64-emit c "addq %rcx, %rax") "o" x64-fail-past-fixnum))
                  ((string=? n "-") (x64-failing-if (x64-emit c "subq %rcx, %rax") "o" x64-fail-past-fixnum))
                  ((string=? n "*") (x64-failing-if (x64-emit (x64-emit c "sarq $3, %rax") "imulq %rcx, %rax") "o" x64-fail-past-fixnum))
                  ;; Two words from the heap, `%r12` its next free one and `%r13` its
                  ;; end; past it, the collector called, the car and cdr kept on
                  ;; the stack for it (C453).
                  ((string=? n "cons")
                   (let* ((c (x64-allocating c "leaq 16(%r12), %rdx" "    pushq %rax\n    pushq %rcx\n" "    popq %rcx\n    popq %rax\n"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movq %rax, 0(%r12)"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movq %rcx, 8(%r12)"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "leaq 1(%r12), %rax")))
                     (x64-emit c "movq %rdx, %r12")))
                  ((string=? n "string-ref")
                   ;; The index checked against the length, unsigned, so that one
                   ;; below 0 is past it too; then the word of its code point, the
                   ;; low half or the high, made a character (C421).
                   (let* ((k (x64-fresh-label c)) (bad (x64-label c "fail" k)) (even (x64-label c "even" k)) (past (x64-label c "ref" k))
                          (c (x64-labelled c))
                          (c (x64-emit c "sarq $3, %rcx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "cmpq -4(%rax), %rcx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c (string-append "jae " bad)))
                          (c (tagcase c (x64-code (ls n2 slots fs px)
                                          (x64-code ls n2 slots (cons (string-list-append (list bad ":\n    movq -4(%rax), %rdi\n    call kc_string_index_fail\n")) fs) px))))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movq %rcx, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "shrq $1, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movq 4(%rax,%rdx,8), %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "testq $1, %rcx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c (string-append "jz " even)))
                          (c (x64-emit c "shrq $32, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c (string-append "jmp " past)))
                          (c (x64-emit-label c even))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movl %edx, %edx"))
                          (c (x64-emit-label c past))
                          (c (x64-emit c "shlq $8, %rdx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "orq $67, %rdx")))
                     (x64-emit c "movq %rdx, %rax")))
                  ((string=? n "array-ref") (x64-emit (x64-array-index c) "movq -20(%rsi), %rax"))
                  ((string=? n "make-array")
                   ;; `%rax` the length, `%rcx` the value: a bloblet of kind 32 of
                   ;; as many fields and a trailer (Fixpt's `make-array`,
                   ;; `%make-bloblet-filled`), from the heap; each field the value.
                   (let* ((k (x64-fresh-label c)) (loop (x64-label c "fill" k)) (done (x64-label c "filled" k)) (bad (x64-label c "fail" k))
                          (c (x64-labelled c))
                          (c (x64-emit c "sarq $3, %rax"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "testq %rax, %rax"))
                          (c (x64-emit c (string-append "js " bad)))
                          (c (tagcase c (x64-code (ls n2 slots fs px)
                                          (x64-code ls n2 slots (cons (string-list-append (list bad ":\n    call kc_make_array_fail\n")) fs) px))))
                          ;; The length kept a fixnum while the collector runs.
                          (c (x64-allocating c "leaq 16(%r12,%rax,8), %rdx" "    shlq $3, %rax\n    pushq %rax\n    pushq %rcx\n" "    popq %rcx\n    popq %rax\n    sarq $3, %rax\n"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "leaq 1(%rax), %rsi"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "shlq $14, %rsi"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "orq $262, %rsi"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movq %rsi, 0(%r12)"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movq $1, %rdi"))
                          (c (x64-emit-label c loop))
                          (c (x64-emit c "cmpq %rax, %rdi"))
                          (c (x64-emit c (string-append "ja " done)))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movq %rcx, 0(%r12,%rdi,8)"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "incq %rdi"))
                          (c (x64-emit c (string-append "jmp " loop)))
                          (c (x64-emit-label c done))
                          (c (x64-emit c "leaq 1(%rax), %rsi"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "shlq $3, %rsi"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "orq $5, %rsi"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "movq %rsi, 8(%r12,%rax,8)"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "leaq 4(%rdx), %rax")))
                     (x64-emit c "movq %rdx, %r12")))
                  ((string=? n "set") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rcx, -20(%rax)") "movq $27, %rax"))
                  ((string=? n "string=?") (x64-calling c "kc_string_eq"))
                  ((string=? n "string<?") (x64-calling c "kc_string_lt"))
                  ((string=? n "string-append") (x64-calling c "kc_string_append"))
                  ;; A quasiquote's `,@` (C447): the list copied onto the rest.
                  ((string=? n "append") (x64-calling c "kc_append"))
                  ((string=? n "max") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "cmpq %rcx, %rax") "cmovl %rcx, %rax"))
                  ((string=? n "min") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "cmpq %rcx, %rax") "cmovg %rcx, %rax"))
                  ((or (string=? n "quotient") (string=? n "remainder") (string=? n "modulo"))
                   (let* ((c (x64-emit c "testq %rcx, %rcx"))
                          (c (x64-failing-if c "e" x64-fail-division))
                          (c (x64-emit c "sarq $3, %rax"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "sarq $3, %rcx"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "cqto"))
                          (c (x64-emit c "idivq %rcx")))
                     (cond ((string=? n "quotient")
                            ;; Only the least fixnum by -1 is past a fixnum.
                            (let* ((c (x64-emit c (string-append "movabsq $" (string-append (i64->string x64-fixnum-max) ", %rdx"))))
                                   (c (x64-emit c "cmpq %rdx, %rax"))
                                   (c (x64-failing-if c "g" x64-fail-past-fixnum)))
                              (x64-emit c "shlq $3, %rax")))
                           ((string=? n "remainder") (x64-emit (x64-emit c "movq %rdx, %rax") "shlq $3, %rax"))
                           (else
                            ;; The remainder, of the divisor's sign: where the two
                            ;; differ and it is not 0, the divisor added.
                            (let* ((k (x64-fresh-label c)) (past (x64-label c "mod" k))
                                   (c (x64-labelled c))
                                   (c (x64-emit c "movq %rdx, %rax"))
                                   (c (x64-emit c "testq %rax, %rax"))
                                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "je " past)))
                                   (c (x64-emit c "movq %rax, %rdx"))
                                   (c (x64-emit c "xorq %rcx, %rdx"))
                                   (c (x64-emit c (string-append "jns " past)))
                                   (c (x64-emit c "addq %rcx, %rax"))
                                   (c (x64-emit-label c past)))
                              (x64-emit c "shlq $3, %rax"))))))
                  (else (begin (error (string-append "kc: the native back end has no primitive " n)) c))))))

      "The frame's bytes: its slots, and 8 more if that keeps the stack aligned
       (entered 8 below a multiple of 16, two registers pushed)."
      (define x64-frame (subr kfx (i64) i64)
        (lambda (slots) (let ((b (i64* 8 slots))) (if (i64= (i64-remainder b 16) 8) b (i64+ b 8)))))

      "A procedure's frame: its slots, rounded so that, entered 8 below a
       multiple of 16, it calls at one."
      (define x64-frame-of-call (subr kfx (i64) i64)
        (lambda (slots) (let ((b (i64* 8 slots))) (if (i64= (i64-remainder b 16) 8) b (i64+ b 8)))))

      "`asm-item PATH KEY`: a form's code (C407), `(asm SLOTS CODE FAILS)`: a
       procedure's whole function, its frame in it; a value definition's or an
       expression's code for `kc_entry`, as many slots as it uses, and what it
       ends with (a definition's value stored in its cell; an expression's value
       given to the runtime's `kc_show`, which writes it); its failures' calls."
      (define x64-asm-item-text (subr kfx (i64 (listof string acyclic) (listof string acyclic)) string)
        (lambda (slots ls fails)
          (string-list-append
            (list "(asm " (i64->string slots) " "
                  (kc-datum (str (string-list-append (reverse ls)) "" 0)) " "
                  (kc-datum (str (string-list-append (reverse fails)) "" 0)) ")")))))

    (define q-asm-item qbody
      (lambda (d run a-path a-key)
        (let* ((path a-path) (key a-key) (i (l0-item d run path key)) (k (item-kind i))
               (px (x64-name key)))
          (cond ((string=? k "none") "(asm 0 \"\" \"\")")
                ((string=? k "proc")
                 (let* ((ps (item-params i)) (n (size ps)))
                   (if (i64> n x64-most-args)
                       (not-yet path "a procedure of more than 64 parameters")
                       ;; Its body in tail position, its frame `fr`, a symbol set to
                       ;; its size once its code is made (C413).
                       (let ((fr (string-append ".L" (string-append px "_frame"))))
                         (tagcase (x64-emit-tail (x64-loaded-args (x64-stored-params (x64-using (x64-code nil 0 0 nil px) n) x64-arg-registers 0 n) 6 n)
                                                 (item-body i) n (x64-params-at ps 0 nil) fr)
                           (x64-code (ls m slots fails px2)
                             (x64-asm-item-text 0
                               (append ls (list (string-list-append (list "    .globl " (x64-proc-symbol (item-name i)) "\n" (x64-proc-symbol (item-name i)) ":\n    subq $" fr ", %rsp\n"
                                                                          (x64-entry-checks (x64-proc-symbol (item-name i)))
                                                                          (x64-frame-zeroed (x64-frame-of-call slots) 0 nil)))))
                               ;; Its frame made first, its code after (`ls` is newest first).
                               (cons (string-list-append (list (x64-entry-calls (x64-proc-symbol (item-name i))) "    .set " fr ", " (i64->string (x64-frame-of-call slots)) "\n")) fails))))))))
                ((string=? k "global")
                 (tagcase (x64-emit-expr (x64-code nil 0 0 nil px) (item-body i) 0 nil)
                   (x64-code (ls m slots fails px2)
                     (x64-asm-item-text slots (cons (x64-cell-stored "%rax" (x64-global-symbol (item-name i))) ls) fails))))
                (else
                 (tagcase (x64-emit-expr (x64-code nil 0 0 nil px) (item-body i) 0 nil)
                   (x64-code (ls m slots fails px2)
                     (x64-asm-item-text slots (cons "    movq %rax, %rdi\n    call kc_show\n" ls) fails))))))))

    (hide
      (define x64-asm-of (subr qe (db runner string string) sexp)
        (lambda (d run path key) (car (read-all (db-get d run (key2 "asm-item" path key)) "asm" 1))))

      (define x64-part (subr kfx (sexp i64) string)
        (lambda (x i) (tagcase (sexp-at (items x) i) (str (s f p) s) (else other ""))))

      (define x64-slots-of (subr kfx (sexp) i64)
        (lambda (x) (tagcase (second (items x)) (num (k f p) k) (else other 0))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-max-slots (subr kfx (sexps i64) i64)
          (lambda (xs m) (if (null? xs) m (x64-max-slots (cdr xs) (let ((k (x64-slots-of (car xs)))) (if (i64> k m) k m))))))))

    (hide
      (define-rec
        (x64-applies? (subr kfx ((listof string acyclic) (listof string acyclic)) bool)
          (lambda (kinds names)
            "Whether the program defines `%phase1-apply`, a procedure (C448)."
            (cond ((or (null? kinds) (null? names)) #f)
                  ((and (string=? (car kinds) "proc") (string=? (car names) "%phase1-apply")) #t)
                  (else (x64-applies? (cdr kinds) (cdr names)))))))

      "A routine of kcrt's that makes something in kc's heap (C455): kc's
       code calls `name`, its `n` arguments in `%rdi`, `%rsi`, `%rdx`, as it
       calls any routine; this puts them in stack words of its own, a 0 for
       each not given, so that the collector moves what they hold, puts the
       heap's next free word and its stack pointer in the block, and calls
       kcrt's routine `rt` on those words and the block (`kc_gc`, the
       state block's words from 688, C466), which takes its room by kcrt-core's `gc::words`,
       collecting if need be, and reads its arguments after; the heap the
       block has then made `%r12` and `%r13`."
      (define x64-heap-routine (subr kfx (string string i64) string)
        (lambda (name rt n)
          (string-list-append
            (list "    .text\n    .globl " name "\n" name ":\n    subq $24, %rsp\n    movq %rdi, 0(%rsp)\n"
                  (if (i64< n 2) "    movq $0, 8(%rsp)\n" "    movq %rsi, 8(%rsp)\n")
                  (if (i64< n 3) "    movq $0, 16(%rsp)\n" "    movq %rdx, 16(%rsp)\n")
                  "    leaq 688(%r15), %rsi\n"
                  "    movq %r12, 40(%rsi)\n    movq %rsp, 48(%rsi)\n    movq %rsp, %rdi\n"
                  "    call " rt "\n    movq 728(%r15), %r12\n    movq 696(%r15), %r13\n    addq $24, %rsp\n    ret\n"))))

      "What `kc_entry`'s object gives the runtime besides (C448): the heap's
       next free word, kept there when `kc_entry` returns (`kc_heap_next`,
       the state block's word 680, C466);
       `kc_call2`, which calls a procedure of kc's code on two arguments, the
       heap in `%r12` and `%r13` as kc's code has it, and keeps the heap's
       next word after; and `kc_apply_address`, which gives `%phase1-apply`'s
       address if the program defines it (a transformer's, kayak-kcrt's
       `--apply`), else 0: made relative to the code, so that an image needs
       no absolute address (C454; it was a word, `kc_apply_entry`).

       And the collector's (C453): `kc_gc`, its block, the state block's
       words from 688 (C466), as kcrt-core's `gc.rs` reads it (the space's
       first word and its end, the stack's base, the globals' cells' run,
       the cells' addresses the writable view's),
       which `kc_gc_init` fills at `kc_entry` (its stack's base the
       entry's, past its saved registers) and `kc_call2` gives its own
       base; `kc_gc_call`, which kc's code calls where an allocation does
       not fit, given its bytes in `%rdi`: kcrt's `kc_collect` given them,
       the caller's stack pointer and the block, the heap it gives back
       made `%r12` and `%r13`. Its words, besides: the heap's next free word
       and the stack pointer of a routine that makes something there
       (C455, `x64-heap-routine`), whose wrappers are here, so that a
       program built and one in process call kcrt the same way.

       And delimited control's (C458): `kc_prompts`, the state block's
       word 664 (C466), the innermost prompt's record (`x64-emit-prompt`), none at `kc_entry` (`kc_gc_init`); and
       `kc_abort`, given the tag in `%rdi` and the value in `%rsi`, which
       finds that tag's innermost prompt by `eq?` (a tag is a box, Fixpt's),
       takes it and those inside it off, makes the stack pointer the
       record's and jumps to its handler's call with the value; no prompt
       of the tag, failure 10, Fixpt's native machines' words.

       And capture's (C459), as Fixpt's native convention takes a
       continuation (`docs/research/native-conventions.md`, step 5): the
       frames from the capture's return up to its tag's prompt's, copied
       into the heap. `kc_capture`, given the procedure, the tag, and 8 if
       the continuation may be resumed once only: in stack words of its own
       those, the innermost prompt, `kc_resume`'s address and that flag;
       kcrt's `kcrt_capture` makes the copy and a closure over it of
       `kc_resume` (collecting if need be, the words moved), and the
       procedure is called on it in tail position, so that it returns to
       the capture's caller. `kc_resume`, the closure's code (in `%r10`,
       the value in `%rdi`, aligned so that its address reads as a
       fixnum): the copy put back below its caller's return, the stack
       pointer first moved past where it goes so that kcrt's
       `kcrt_resume_copy` runs below it, which puts the copy's prompts'
       records on the current ones; then the capture's return taken with
       the value, so that the copy's last return is to the resume's caller
       (a composable continuation's composition). Past the stack's limit,
       failure 8. A whole one (`cwcc`, C460, its flag 32) is the frames up
       to the run's (`kc_run_base`, the stack pointer of the frame each
       top-level form's run is called from: `kc_entry`'s, or `kc_call2`'s),
       put back below the current run's return, whatever is there now
       given up, so that it returns where the current run does, as
       Fixpt's.

       And marks' (C460), each a record on the prompts' chain, as Fixpt's
       native convention has a mark a frame of its own: the record before,
       the key, its own address (a stack address, as a prompt's stack
       pointer is, which a capture makes an offset), the value, and a word
       for the stack's alignment. `kc_with_mark` (the key, the value and
       the thunk): where it was called to return to `kc_mark_ret` (in tail
       position under a mark) and that mark's key is this, its value
       replaced; else a record pushed, `kc_mark_ret` as its return, which
       takes it off. Then the thunk tail-called. `kc_first_mark` walks the
       chain for the key; `kc_current_marks` and `kc_marks_of`, kcrt's,
       make the list of a key's marks, the chain's or a continuation's
       copy's, innermost first.

       And `kc_apply_run` (C455; the state in `%rdi`), a transformer's run
       after `kc_entry`, a built one's `--apply` and one in process alike:
       `%phase1-apply` called on the use and the tag kcrt was given
       (`kc_given`, 0 and the fixnum 1, each a string made in kc's heap,
       the first kept in a stack word the collector moves, above a base of
       its own), and its answer written (`kc_show`); a program with none
       failed (`kc_fail`, 9)."
      (define x64-entry-support (subr kfx (bool) string)
        (lambda (applies)
          (string-list-append
            (list "    .text\nkc_gc_init:\n    movq $0, 664(%r15)\n    leaq 8(%rsp), %rax\n"
                  "    movq %r12, 688(%r15)\n    movq %r13, 696(%r15)\n    movq %rax, 704(%r15)\n"
                  "    leaq kc_cells_lo(%rip), %rax\n    subq 208(%r15), %rax\n    subq $4, %rax\n    movq %rax, 712(%r15)\n"
                  "    leaq kc_cells_hi(%rip), %rax\n    subq 208(%r15), %rax\n    subq $4, %rax\n    movq %rax, 720(%r15)\n    ret\n"
                  "    .globl kc_gc_call\nkc_gc_call:\n    leaq 8(%rsp), %rsi\n    leaq 688(%r15), %rdx\n"
                  "    subq $8, %rsp\n    call kc_collect\n    addq $8, %rsp\n    movq %rax, %r12\n    movq %rdx, %r13\n    ret\n"
                  "    .text\n    .globl kc_abort\nkc_abort:\n    movq 664(%r15), %rax\n"
                  ".Lkc_abort_look:\n    testq %rax, %rax\n    je .Lkc_abort_none\n    cmpq %rdi, 8(%rax)\n    je .Lkc_abort_found\n"
                  "    movq 0(%rax), %rax\n    jmp .Lkc_abort_look\n"
                  ".Lkc_abort_found:\n    movq 0(%rax), %rdx\n" "    movq %rdx, 664(%r15)\n"
                  "    movq 24(%rax), %rcx\n    movq 16(%rax), %rsp\n    movq %rsi, %rax\n    jmp *%rcx\n"
                  ".Lkc_abort_none:\n    subq $8, %rsp\n    movl $10, %edi\n    call kc_fail\n"
                  "    .text\n    .globl kc_capture\nkc_capture:\n    subq $40, %rsp\n    movq %rdi, 0(%rsp)\n    movq %rsi, 8(%rsp)\n"
                  "    movq 664(%r15), %rax\n    movq %rax, 16(%rsp)\n    leaq kc_resume(%rip), %rax\n    movq %rax, 24(%rsp)\n    movq %rdx, 32(%rsp)\n"
                  "    leaq 688(%r15), %rsi\n    movq %r12, 40(%rsi)\n    movq %rsp, 48(%rsi)\n    movq %rsp, %rdi\n"
                  "    call kcrt_capture\n    movq 728(%r15), %r12\n    movq 696(%r15), %r13\n"
                  "    movq 0(%rsp), %r10\n    movq %rax, %rdi\n    addq $40, %rsp\n    jmp *-28(%r10)\n"
                  "    .p2align 3\n    .globl kc_resume\nkc_resume:\n    movq -36(%r10), %r11\n    movq -20(%r11), %rax\n    movq -36(%r11), %rcx\n    andq $32, %rcx\n"
                  "    jne .Lkc_resume_whole\n    movq %rsp, %rcx\n    jmp .Lkc_resume_at\n"
                  ".Lkc_resume_whole:\n    movq 672(%r15), %rcx\n    subq $8, %rcx\n"
                  ".Lkc_resume_at:\n    subq %rax, %rcx\n"
                  "    cmpq 16(%r15), %rcx\n    jb .Lkc_resume_deep\n    movq %rdi, -8(%rcx)\n    movq %rsp, %rdx\n    cmpq %rdx, %rcx\n    jae .Lkc_resume_low\n    movq %rcx, %rdx\n"
                  ".Lkc_resume_low:\n    leaq -64(%rdx), %rsp\n    andq $-16, %rsp\n    movq %rcx, 8(%rsp)\n"
                  "    movq %r11, %rdi\n    movq %rcx, %rsi\n    movq 664(%r15), %rdx\n    call kcrt_resume_copy\n    andq $-2, %rax\n    movq %rax, %rdx\n"
                  "    movq %rdx, 664(%r15)\n"
                  "    movq 8(%rsp), %rcx\n    movq %rcx, %rsp\n    movq -8(%rcx), %rax\n    ret\n"
                  ".Lkc_resume_deep:\n    subq $8, %rsp\n    movl $8, %edi\n    call kc_fail\n"
                  "    .text\n    .globl kc_with_mark\nkc_with_mark:\n    leaq kc_mark_ret(%rip), %rax\n    cmpq %rax, 0(%rsp)\n    jne .Lkc_mark_push\n"
                  "    cmpq %rdi, 16(%rsp)\n    jne .Lkc_mark_push\n    movq %rsi, 32(%rsp)\n    movq %rdx, %r10\n    jmp *-28(%r10)\n"
                  ".Lkc_mark_push:\n    subq $40, %rsp\n    movq 664(%r15), %rcx\n    movq %rcx, 0(%rsp)\n    movq %rdi, 8(%rsp)\n    movq %rsp, 16(%rsp)\n"
                  "    movq %rsi, 24(%rsp)\n    movq $0, 32(%rsp)\n" "    movq %rsp, 664(%r15)\n"
                  "    leaq kc_mark_ret(%rip), %rax\n    pushq %rax\n    movq %rdx, %r10\n    jmp *-28(%r10)\n"
                  "kc_mark_ret:\n    movq 0(%rsp), %rdx\n" "    movq %rdx, 664(%r15)\n" "    addq $40, %rsp\n    ret\n"
                  "    .globl kc_first_mark\nkc_first_mark:\n    movq 664(%r15), %rax\n"
                  ".Lkc_fm_look:\n    testq %rax, %rax\n    je .Lkc_fm_none\n    cmpq %rdi, 8(%rax)\n    je .Lkc_fm_found\n    movq 0(%rax), %rax\n    jmp .Lkc_fm_look\n"
                  ".Lkc_fm_found:\n    movq 24(%rax), %rax\n    ret\n.Lkc_fm_none:\n    movq %rsi, %rax\n    ret\n"
                  (x64-heap-routine "kc_current_marks" "kcrt_current_marks" 2)
                  (x64-heap-routine "kc_marks_of" "kcrt_marks_of" 2)
                  "    .text\n    .globl kc_apply_address\nkc_apply_address:\n"
                  (if applies (string-append "    leaq " (string-append (x64-proc-symbol "%phase1-apply") "(%rip), %rax\n")) "    movl $0, %eax\n")
                  "    ret\n"
                  "    .text\n    .globl kc_call2\nkc_call2:\n    pushq %r15\n    pushq %r13\n    pushq %r12\n    movq %r8, %r15\n"
                  "    movq 680(%r15), %r12\n    movq 696(%r15), %r13\n    movq %rsp, 704(%r15)\n"
                  "    movq %rsp, 672(%r15)\n"
                  "    movq %rdi, %rax\n    movq %rsi, %rdi\n    movq %rdx, %rsi\n"
                  "    call *%rax\n" "    movq %r12, 680(%r15)\n" "    popq %r12\n    popq %r13\n    popq %r15\n    ret\n"
                  (x64-heap-routine "kc_string_append" "kcrt_string_append" 2)
                  (x64-heap-routine "kc_substring" "kcrt_substring" 3)
                  (x64-heap-routine "kc_append" "kcrt_append" 2)
                  (x64-heap-routine "kc_reverse" "kcrt_reverse" 1)
                  (x64-heap-routine "kc_int_to_string" "kcrt_int_to_string" 1)
                  (x64-heap-routine "kc_char_to_string" "kcrt_char_to_string" 1)
                  (x64-heap-routine "kc_f64_to_string" "kcrt_f64_to_string" 1)
                  (x64-heap-routine "kc_list_to_vector" "kcrt_list_to_vector" 1)
                  (x64-heap-routine "kc_given" "kcrt_given" 1)
                  "    .text\n    .globl kc_apply_run\nkc_apply_run:\n    pushq %r15\n    pushq %r13\n    pushq %r12\n    movq %rdi, %r15\n"
                  "    call kc_apply_address\n    testq %rax, %rax\n    jne .Lkc_apply_have\n    movl $9, %edi\n    call kc_fail\n"
                  ".Lkc_apply_have:\n    subq $16, %rsp\n    movq %rax, 0(%rsp)\n    movq $0, 8(%rsp)\n"
                  "    movq 680(%r15), %r12\n    movq 696(%r15), %r13\n"
                  "    leaq 16(%rsp), %rax\n    movq %rax, 704(%r15)\n"
                  "    movl $0, %edi\n    call kc_given\n    movq %rax, 8(%rsp)\n    movl $8, %edi\n    call kc_given\n    movq %rax, %rdx\n"
                  "    movq %r12, 680(%r15)\n"
                  "    movq 8(%rsp), %rsi\n    movq 0(%rsp), %rdi\n    movl $0, %ecx\n    movq %r15, %r8\n"
                  "    call kc_call2\n    movq %rax, %rdi\n    call kc_show\n    addq $16, %rsp\n    popq %r12\n    popq %r13\n    popq %r15\n    ret\n")))))

    "The runtime's procedures kc's code calls, in order: in process, each
     a cell of the table of their addresses (C452, `x64-run-support`)."
    (define x64-services strings
      (list "kc_show" "kc_fail" "kc_intern" "kc_string_eq" "kc_string_lt" "kcrt_string_append"
            "kcrt_substring" "kc_symbol_to_string" "kc_is_string" "kc_is_symbol" "kc_is_procedure"
            "kc_is_kind" "kcrt_append" "kc_array_index_fail" "kc_make_array_fail" "kc_string_index_fail" "kc_collect"
            "kcrt_given" "kc_gc_reset" "kcrt_capture" "kcrt_resume_copy" "kcrt_current_marks" "kcrt_marks_of"
            "kcrt_reverse" "kcrt_int_to_string"
            "kcrt_char_to_string" "kc_char_whitespace" "kc_char_numeric" "kc_string_hash" "kc_symbol_hash"
            "kcrt_f64_to_string" "kcrt_list_to_vector" "kc_error"))

    (hide
      "Routines that always fail, and those that may (C452): each called,
       not jumped to, so that its answer is seen."
      (define x64-failing strings (list "kc_fail" "kc_array_index_fail" "kc_make_array_fail" "kc_string_index_fail" "kc_error"))
      (define x64-may-fail strings (list "kcrt_string_append" "kcrt_substring" "kcrt_append" "kcrt_given" "kc_collect" "kcrt_capture" "kcrt_resume_copy" "kcrt_current_marks" "kcrt_marks_of" "kcrt_reverse" "kcrt_int_to_string"
                                         "kcrt_char_to_string" "kcrt_f64_to_string" "kcrt_list_to_vector"))

      (define-rec
        (x64-routine-stubs (subr kfx (strings i64 (listof string acyclic)) string)
          (lambda (ns k acc)
            (if (null? ns)
                (string-list-append (reverse acc))
                (let ((cell (string-append "kc_routines+" (i64->string (i64* 8 k)))))
                  (x64-routine-stubs (cdr ns) (i64+ k 1)
                    (cons (string-list-append
                            (cond ((string-member? (car ns) x64-failing)
                                   (list (car ns) ":\n    subq $8, %rsp\n    call *" cell "(%rip)\n    jmp kc_failed\n"))
                                  ((string-member? (car ns) x64-may-fail)
                                   (list (car ns) ":\n    subq $8, %rsp\n    call *" cell "(%rip)\n    addq $8, %rsp\n"
                                         "    testq %rax, %rax\n    je kc_failed\n    ret\n"))
                                  (else (list (car ns) ":\n    jmp *" cell "(%rip)\n"))))
                          acc)))))))

      (define-rec
        (x64-quads (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic) (listof string acyclic)) string)
          (lambda (xs acc)
            (if (null? xs) (string-list-append (reverse acc)) (x64-quads (cdr xs) (cons (string-append "    .quad " (string-append (i64->string (car xs)) "\n")) acc)))))))

    "What kc's code runs on in process (C451), before the program (`asm`),
     so that its first byte is the code bloblet's: the code's field before
     it, as Fixpt's, field 0 (16 bytes back) the heap, an `i64` flat array
     shared with KFX.

     `kc_native_entry`, as Fixpt's native convention enters code (the state
     in `%r15`, the heap's array in `%rdi`, its first element's address
     less the tag 4): the array's words 0 and 1 made its own address and
     the code's; the heap from word 16 to the length KFX put in word 3; its
     stack pointer to word 4; the collector's spaces of a run before
     dropped (C454, `kc_gc_reset`: the run's region, the array's heap
     used again from its start); then `kc_entry`, and 0 back. Where KFX
     put 1 in word 5, a transformer's run (C454, as a built one's
     `--apply`): after `kc_entry`, `kc_apply_run` (C455, a built one's
     too), `%phase1-apply` called on the use and the tag KFX gave, its
     answer written (`kc_show`, whose lines KFX takes).

     The runtime (C452) is kayak-kcrt-core's, a built program's: `addrs`,
     each routine's address in order (`x64-services`), a table
     (`kc_routines`) each stub jumps through, as Fixpt's code calls its
     Rust through addresses it is given. A routine that fails keeps its
     words and answers 0 (kcrt's `here_…`): its stub calls it, and goes to
     `kc_failed`, which goes back past kc's frames to the entry's, the
     stack pointer word 4 kept, and so to the trampoline, 1 back (kc's own
     convention's failure; kayak-jit's traps end the program a KFX error,
     which nothing of `kc run`'s could catch, an `attempt` doing no
     output)."
    (define x64-run-support (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic)) string)
      (lambda (addrs)
        (string-list-append
          (list "    .text\nkc_native_entry:\n    pushq %rbp\n    leaq -4(%rdi), %rax\n    movq %rax, 0(%rax)\n"
                "    leaq kc_native_entry(%rip), %rcx\n    movq %rcx, 8(%rax)\n    movq 24(%rax), %rsi\n    shlq $3, %rsi\n"
                "    addq %rax, %rsi\n    leaq 128(%rax), %rdi\n    movq %rsp, 744(%r15)\n    pushq %rdi\n    pushq %rsi\n    call kc_gc_reset\n"
                "    popq %rsi\n    popq %rdi\n    movq %r15, %rdx\n    call kc_entry\n"
                "    movq kc_native_entry-16(%rip), %rcx\n    cmpq $0, 36(%rcx)\n    je .Lkc_native_done\n"
                "    movq %r15, %rdi\n    call kc_apply_run\n"
                ".Lkc_native_done:\n    movl $0, %eax\n    popq %rbp\n    ret\n"
                "kc_failed:\n    movq 744(%r15), %rsp\n    movl $8, %eax\n    popq %rbp\n    ret\n"
                (x64-routine-stubs x64-services 0 nil)
                "    .data\n    .p2align 3\nkc_routines:\n" (x64-quads addrs nil) "    .text\n"))))

    "A global's cell: in `.bss`, `.globl`, so that a procedure in an object of
     its own (`kc build`, C419) reads it."
    (define x64-cell (subr kfx (string) string)
      (lambda (n) (string-list-append (list "    .globl " (x64-global-symbol n) "\n" (x64-global-symbol n) ":\n    .quad 0\n"))))

    "`asm PATH`: the program: each global's cell; each procedure; then
     `kc_entry`, which keeps the heap in `%r12` and `%r13` and makes the
     value definitions and expressions in order."
    (define q-asm qbody
      (lambda (d run path a-key)
        (let* ((keys (kc-keys d run path))
               (its (kc-items-of d run "asm-item" path keys))
               (l0s (kc-items-of d run "l0-item" path keys))
               (kinds (map item-kind l0s))
               (names (map item-name l0s))
               (frame (x64-frame (x64-max-slots (filter (lambda ((x sexp)) (i64> (x64-slots-of x) -1)) its) 0))))
          (string-list-append
            (append (list "# Made by kc (docs/research/kc.md) from " path ".\n    .bss\n    .p2align 3\nkc_cells_lo:\n")
             (append (map2 (lambda ((k string) (n string)) (if (string=? k "global") (x64-cell n) "")) kinds names)
              (append (list "kc_cells_hi:\n    .text\n")
               (append (map2 (lambda ((k string) (x sexp)) (if (string=? k "proc") (string-append (x64-part x 2) (x64-part x 3)) "")) kinds its)
                (append (list "    .globl kc_entry\nkc_entry:\n    pushq %r15\n    pushq %r14\n    pushq %r13\n    pushq %r12\n    movq %rdi, %r12\n    movq %rsi, %r13\n    movq %rdx, %r15\n"
                              "    call kc_gc_init\n    subq $" (i64->string frame) ", %rsp\n" (x64-frame-zeroed frame 0 nil)
                              "    movq %rsp, 672(%r15)\n")
                 (append (map2 (lambda ((k string) (x sexp)) (if (string=? k "proc") "" (x64-part x 2))) kinds its)
                  (append (list "    movq %r12, 680(%r15)\n" "    addq $" (i64->string frame) ", %rsp\n    popq %r12\n    popq %r13\n    popq %r14\n    popq %r15\n    ret\n")
                   (append (map2 (lambda ((k string) (x sexp)) (if (string=? k "proc") "" (x64-part x 3))) kinds its)
                           (list (x64-entry-support (x64-applies? kinds names)) "    .section .note.GNU-stack,\"\",@progbits\n")))))))))))))

    "`asm-entry PATH` (C419): the object of what is no procedure's: each
     global's cell; `kc_entry`, which keeps the heap in `%r12` and `%r13` and
     makes the value definitions and expressions in order; their failures'
     calls. With each procedure's object (`x64-object-text`), what `asm`
     writes as one file, `kc build` assembles apart."
    (define q-asm-entry qbody
      (lambda (d run path a-key)
        (let* ((keys (kc-keys d run path))
               (ifs (kc-items-of d run "interface" path keys))
               (kinds (map item-kind ifs))
               (names (map item-name ifs))
               (rest (x64-not-procs keys kinds nil))
               (its (kc-items-of d run "asm-item" path rest))
               (frame (x64-frame (x64-max-slots (filter (lambda ((x sexp)) (i64> (x64-slots-of x) -1)) its) 0))))
          (string-list-append
            (append (list "# Made by kc (docs/research/kc.md) from " path ".\n    .bss\n    .p2align 3\nkc_cells_lo:\n")
             (append (map2 (lambda ((k string) (n string)) (if (string=? k "value") (x64-cell n) "")) kinds names)
              (append (list "kc_cells_hi:\n    .text\n    .globl kc_entry\nkc_entry:\n    pushq %r15\n    pushq %r14\n    pushq %r13\n    pushq %r12\n    movq %rdi, %r12\n    movq %rsi, %r13\n    movq %rdx, %r15\n"
                            "    call kc_gc_init\n    subq $" (i64->string frame) ", %rsp\n" (x64-frame-zeroed frame 0 nil)
                            "    movq %rsp, 672(%r15)\n")
               (append (map (lambda ((x sexp)) (x64-part x 2)) its)
                (append (list "    movq %r12, 680(%r15)\n" "    addq $" (i64->string frame) ", %rsp\n    popq %r12\n    popq %r13\n    popq %r14\n    popq %r15\n    ret\n")
                 (append (map (lambda ((x sexp)) (x64-part x 3)) its)
                         (list (x64-entry-support (x64-applies? kinds names)) "    .section .note.GNU-stack,\"\",@progbits\n")))))))))))

    "A procedure's object's assembly (C419), of its `asm-item`."
    (define x64-object-text (subr kfx (sexp) string)
      (lambda (x)
        (string-list-append (list "    .text\n" (x64-part x 2) (x64-part x 3) "    .section .note.GNU-stack,\"\",@progbits\n"))))

    (hide
      (define-rec
        (x64-not-procs (subr kfx ((listof string acyclic) (listof string acyclic) (listof string acyclic)) (listof string acyclic))
          (lambda (ks kinds acc)
            (cond ((or (null? ks) (null? kinds)) (reverse acc))
                  ((string=? (car kinds) "proc") (x64-not-procs (cdr ks) (cdr kinds) acc))
                  (else (x64-not-procs (cdr ks) (cdr kinds) (cons (car ks) acc)))))))

      "How many procedures an object holds, at most (C419): one each would
       start the assembler once for each and give the linker as many (25 s
       cold at 5000 procedures); a run of them, in order, reassembled whole
       when one of them changes."
      (define x64-chunk i64 64)

      (define-rec
        (x64-object-lines (subr qe (db runner string (listof string acyclic) (listof string acyclic) (listof string acyclic) i64 i64 (listof string acyclic)) (listof string acyclic))
          (lambda (d run path ks kinds members n fp acc)
            "The objects: each a run of up to `x64-chunk` procedures, in order,
             `((KEY ...) FP)`, FP its members' code's fingerprints folded."
            (let ((done (lambda ((acc (listof string acyclic)))
                          (if (null? members)
                              acc
                              (cons (string-list-append (list "((" (words-of (map (lambda ((k string)) (kc-datum (str k "" 0))) (reverse members))) ") " (i64->string fp) ")")) acc)))))
              (cond ((or (null? ks) (null? kinds)) (reverse (done acc)))
                    ((not (string=? (car kinds) "proc")) (x64-object-lines d run path (cdr ks) (cdr kinds) members n fp acc))
                    ((i64>= n x64-chunk) (x64-object-lines d run path ks kinds nil 0 (with queries fnv-offset) (done acc)))
                    (else
                     (x64-object-lines d run path (cdr ks) (cdr kinds) (cons (car ks) members) (i64+ n 1)
                                       ((with queries fnv-i64) (db-get-fingerprint d run (key2 "asm-item" path (car ks))) fp)
                                       acc))))))))

    "`objects PATH` (C419): the program's objects, each by the fingerprint of
     what it is assembled from, read without that being read: `((KEY ...)
     FP)` of each run of procedures (their `asm-item`s'), then `(() FP)` of
     what is no procedure's (`asm-entry`'s). An edit that leaves every
     procedure's code as it was leaves this as it was."
    (define q-objects qbody
      (lambda (d run path a-key)
        (let* ((keys (kc-keys d run path))
               (kinds (map item-kind (kc-items-of d run "interface" path keys))))
          (string-list-append
            (append (list "(")
              (append (x64-object-lines d run path keys kinds nil 0 (with queries fnv-offset) nil)
                (list "(() " (i64->string (db-get-fingerprint d run (key1 "asm-entry" path))) "))")))))))))
